  "hindi": "काटती हुई, मानो पिनाक धारण करती हुई, वह चारों ओर बिखरती हुई चली जाए। चारों ओर, पुनः उत्पन्न होने वाली के द्वारा, बुरा चाहने वाले मन में असफल रहें।",
  "english": "Let the cutting one go apart in all directions, bearing a pināka, as it were. On every side, by the again-becoming one, the evil-minded are unprospered in mind.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Low confidence: the subject of etu, the referent of punarbhū and the sense of 'viṣvak punarbhuvā' are not stated in the unit. pināka is kept as a name for a staff or bow. 'manaḥ asamṛddhāḥ' is read as 'unprospered in mind'.",
